 g2)\nL683@P14: ) g1\nL684@P14: Finally, it is also reasonably easy to convert a TG’ term graph into a Jungle with Fin k as Inner node set\nL685@P14: and as Edge set, where k is the number of Let declarations.\nL686@P14: 8 Conclusion and Outlook\nL687@P14: Formalising mathematical definitions of term graphs and their operations in Agda is a remarkably straight\u0002forward exercise, and, due to the dependent typing of Agda, also carries over to typed term graphs much\nL688@P14: more easily than in the more restricted type systems of Haskell or higher-order logic.\nL689@P14: The remarkable abstract interface to variable binding provided by Pouillard and Pottier’s NotSoFresh\nL690@P14: Agda library [PP10] also makes name-binding representations of term graphs conveniently accessible\nL691@P14: to mechanised reasoning and programmed manipulation. Typing is easily added to our TG and TG′\nL692@P14: datatypes — the original Tm datatype provided as NotSoFresh example includes typing, but we omitted\nL693@P14: it here to improve readability.\nL694@P14: Implementing additional term graph operations, manipulations, and conversion functions, and prov\u0002ing the algebraic properties of the term graph operations is ongoing work.\nL695@P14: Future work will strive to base code-graph based optimised-code generation algorithms for the Co\u0002conut project [AK09a] on our Agda formalisations of code graphs, with a fully verifying tool chain as\nL696@P14: ultimate goal.\nL697@P14: References\nL698@P14: [AK94] Zena M. Ariola & Jan Willem Klop (1994): Cyclic Lambda Graph Rewriting. In: Proceedings, Ninth\nL699@P14: Annual IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science. IEEE Computer Society Press, Paris, France,\nL700@P14: pp. 416–425.\nL701@P14: [AK08] Christopher Kumar Anand & Wolfram Kahl (2008): Code Graph Transformations for Verifiable Gen\u0002eration of SIMD-Parallel Assembly Code. In Andy Schürr, Manfred Nagl & Albert Zündorf, editors:\nL702@P14: Applications of Graph Transformations with Industrial Relevance, AGTIVE 2007. LNCS 5088, pp.\nL703@P14-15: 217–232, doi:10.1007/978-3-540-89020-1.Wolfram Kahl 53\nL704@P15: [AK09a] Christopher K. Anand & Wolfram Kahl (2009): An Optimized Cell BE Special Function Library Gen\u0002erated by Coconut. IEEE Transactions on Computers 58(8), pp. 1126–1138, doi:10.1109/TC.2008.\nL705@P15: 223.\nL706@P15: [AK09b] Christopher K. Anand & Wolfram Kahl (2009): Synthesizing and Verifying Multicore Parallelism in\nL707@P15: Categories of Nested Code Graphs. In Michael Alexander & William Gardner, editors: Process Algebra\nL708@P15: for Parallel and Distributed Processing, chapter 1. CRC Computational Science Series 2, Chapman &\nL709@P15: Hall, pp. 3–45.\nL710@P15: [CG99] Andrea Corradini & Fabio Gadducci (1999): An Algebraic Presentation of Term Graphs, via GS\u0002Monoidal Categories. Applied Categorical Structures 7(4), pp. 299–331.\nL711@P15: [CR93] Andrea Corradini & Francesca Rossi (1993): Hyperedge replacement jungle rewriting for term\u0002rewriting systems and logic programming. In B. Courcelle & G. Rozenberg, editors: Selected Papers of\nL712@P15: the International Workshop on Computing by Graph Transformation, Bordeaux, France, March 21–23,\nL713@P15: 1991. Elsevier, pp. 7–48, doi:10.1016/0304-3975(93)90063-Y. Theoretical Computer Science 109\nL714@P15: (1–2).\nL715@P15: [FS90] Peter J. Freyd & Andre Scedrov (1990): Categories, Allegories. North-Holland Mathematical Li\u0002brary 39, North-Holland, Amsterdam.\nL716@P15: [Gon06] Carlos Gonzalía (2006): Relations in Dependent Type Theory. Ph.D. thesis, Department of Computer\nL717@P15: Science and Engineering, Chalmers University of Technology, Göteborg University. Technical Report\nL718@P15: No. 14D.\nL719@P15: [HFBV97] Armando Haeberer, Marcelo Frias, Gabriel Baum & Paulo Veloso (1997): Fork Algebras. In Chris\nL720@P15: Brink, Wolfram Kahl & Gunther Schmidt, editors: Relational Methods in Computer Science, chapter 4.\nL721@P15: Advances in Computing